स्थाल n. plate, dish, vessel, tooth-hole;
 f. स्थाली॑
(earthen) pot, kettle.

स्थाणु॑ a. standing, firm, immovable;
 m. trunk or stem of a
tree, post, pillar, E. of Śiva.

स्था॑न n. standing, remaining, abiding, not budging;
continuation, duration;
 state. condition, position, rank, dignity;
shape, form, appearance;
 sphere, domain, province;
 abode, place, seat,
home, stead (loc. w. gen. or —˚ instead of);
 proper place or time,
occasion or object for (gen. or —˚);
 place of articulation, organ (g.);
the (4) stamina of a kingdom (treasury etc.).

स्थानक m. N. of a man. n. position, attitude;
 rank,
dignity;
 place, spot.

स्थानिन् a. having the first or the right place;
 m. the
primitive element (g.).

स्थापन a. establishing, fixing, settling, founding;
 n.
& f. आ the act of establishing etc.

1 स्था॑मन् n. standing-place, stand;
 stability, strength,
power.

स्थायिन् a. standing, abiding, being in, at, or on (—˚),
present;
 steady, constant, faithful, true.

स्थायुक a. standing, staying in (—˚);
 constant,
durable.

स्थावर॑ a. standing, immovable, firm, lasting,
constant;
 vegetable, belonging to the vegetable world. m. mountain;
 m.
n. sgl. & pl. the vegetable kingdom;
 n. immovable property.
